{"cell": "all-meaning", "word": "whole verse", "type": "meaning", "topic": "whole verse · meaning", "words": ["*"], "view": "In a neighboring passage, maqt means hatred, and the hated person may be called mamqūt or maqīt.", "rows": ["TABRISI:35:36-37/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "all-readings", "word": "whole verse", "type": "readings", "topic": "whole verse · readings", "words": ["*"], "view": "In a neighboring passage, some read bayyinah singular, pointing to scripture or what the Prophet brought; others read bayyināt plural for each prophet's proof or several forms of scriptural evidence.", "rows": ["TABRISI:35:36-37/r2"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "all-links", "word": "whole verse", "type": "links", "topic": "whole verse · links", "words": ["*"], "view": "The preceding comparison of believers and unbelievers leads into the contrast of God's power with idols and the outcome of disbelief.", "rows": ["STUDYQURAN:35:intro/r9"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "all-links", "word": "whole verse", "type": "links", "topic": "whole verse · links", "words": ["*"], "view": "Without faith and righteous deeds, wealth and children increase ruin; worldly possessions and family are vulnerable, whereas the faithful receive manifold reward and enduring safety in the chambers.", "rows": ["ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-6-2:p306/r2", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-6-2:p306/r3", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-6-2:p306/r4", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-6-2:p306/r5"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w2-meaning", "word": "يَصْطَرِخُونَ (word 2)", "type": "meaning", "topic": "يَصْطَرِخُونَ (word 2) · meaning", "words": ["يَصْطَرِخُونَ"], "view": "Yaṣṭarikhūn means crying aloud and calling for help; ṣarākh is a shout, a ṣārikh may be the caller, and a muṣrikh the helper. A poetic example depicts a frightened caller.", "rows": ["IBNABIHATIM:v10p3184#2/r1", "THALABI:v8p114/r1", "MAWARDI-FULL:v4p476/r1", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v18p432/r1", "WAHIDI-WAJIZ:35:34-37/r4", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v6p424#2/r4", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37/r8", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37/r9", "BAYDAWI-FULL:35:37/r1", "NASAFI-FULL:v3p345#2/r1", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v9p36/r6", "TABATABAI:35:37-38/r1", "DURR-FULL:v7p30/r3"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w2-grammar", "word": "يَصْطَرِخُونَ (word 2)", "type": "grammar", "topic": "يَصْطَرِخُونَ (word 2) · grammar", "words": ["يَصْطَرِخُونَ"], "view": "The verb is an intensive iftiʿāl form of ṣarākh: its original tāʾ becomes emphatic ṭāʾ near ṣād, making an effortful, forceful cry.", "rows": ["TAB-FULL:v19p384/r3", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v18p432/r2", "JISHUMI:v8p5854/r4", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v4p440#2/r7", "TABRISI:35:36-37/r3", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v6p494/r1", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v9p36/r6", "SAMIN-DURR:35:37/r2", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p200#2/r1", "BURSEVI:v7p277#2/r1", "IBNASHUR-FULL:v22p318/r7"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w2-grammar", "word": "يَصْطَرِخُونَ (word 2)", "type": "grammar", "topic": "يَصْطَرِخُونَ (word 2) · grammar", "words": ["يَصْطَرِخُونَ فِيهَا"], "view": "The pronoun refers to the disbelievers in the preceding verse; the clause continues the account of their being in Hell rather than serving as a circumstantial clause.", "rows": ["IBNASHUR-FULL:v22p318/r6"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w2-interpretation", "word": "يَصْطَرِخُونَ (word 2)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "يَصْطَرِخُونَ (word 2) · interpretation", "words": ["يَصْطَرِخُونَ فِيهَا"], "view": "Their screaming in Hell conveys intense suffering and helplessness; the plea that follows explains what they cry out for.", "rows": ["MUQATIL:35:37-39/r1", "JISHUMI:v8p5855/r3", "BIQAI-FULL:v6p229/r1", "IBNASHUR-FULL:v22p318/r7", "TABATABAI:35:37-38/r2"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w2-interpretation", "word": "يَصْطَرِخُونَ (word 2)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "يَصْطَرِخُونَ (word 2) · interpretation", "words": ["يَصْطَرِخُونَ فِيهَا"], "view": "They seek rescue from God, rather than calling to one another in confusion.", "rows": ["ALUSI-FULL:v22p200#2/r2"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w2-interpretation", "word": "يَصْطَرِخُونَ (word 2)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "يَصْطَرِخُونَ (word 2) · interpretation", "words": ["يَصْطَرِخُونَ فِيهَا"], "view": "Their cries obtain no relief: the punishment is not eased before or after they ask.", "rows": ["RAZI-FULL:v26p26#3/r1", "KURANYOLU-TEFSIR:35:36/r1"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w4-grammar", "word": "رَبَّنَآ (word 4)", "type": "grammar", "topic": "رَبَّنَآ (word 4) · grammar", "words": ["رَبَّنَآ"], "view": "An omitted verb of saying introduces 'Our Lord'; the plea may explain their cries, be independent speech, or describe their state circumstantially.", "rows": ["IBNATIYYA-FULL:v4p440#2/r8", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#2/r4", "SAMIN-DURR:35:37/r1", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p200#2/r3"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w4-interpretation", "word": "رَبَّنَآ (word 4)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "رَبَّنَآ (word 4) · interpretation", "words": ["رَبَّنَآ أَخْرِجْنَا"], "view": "They ask God to take them out of Hell and return them to worldly life for another chance to act well.", "rows": ["MUQATIL:35:37-39/r1", "YAHYA-SALLAM:v2p793/r11", "TAB-FULL:v19p384/r2", "THALABI:v8p114/r2", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v18p432/r3", "JISHUMI:v8p5855/r3", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v6p424#2/r4", "QUSHAYRI:v3p71/r1", "TABRISI:35:36-37/r6", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v6p494/r1", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#2/r1", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v9p36/r7", "BIQAI-FULL:v6p229/r1", "BURSEVI:v7p277#2/r2", "BURSEVI:v7p279/r3", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p200#2/r6", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-6-2:p361/r2", "TABATABAI:35:37-38/r3", "STUDYQURAN:35:37/r1"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w4-interpretation", "word": "رَبَّنَآ (word 4)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "رَبَّنَآ (word 4) · interpretation", "words": ["رَبَّنَآ أَخْرِجْنَا نَعْمَلْ صَٰلِحًا"], "view": "Their promise is belated repentance after seeing Resurrection and judgment; their hope for reprieve has become a plea and then a vow to reform.", "rows": ["RAZI-FULL:v26p26#3/r3", "IBNASHUR-FULL:v22p318/r8", "STUDYQURAN:35:37/r1"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w4-interpretation", "word": "رَبَّنَآ (word 4)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "رَبَّنَآ (word 4) · interpretation", "words": ["رَبَّنَآ أَخْرِجْنَا"], "view": "The rejected request shows their suffering is punishment rather than correction; repentance and repair belong to worldly life, and return from the afterlife is impossible.", "rows": ["RAZI-FULL:v26p26#3/r2", "RAZI-FULL:v26p26#3/r5", "JISHUMI:v8p5857/r1", "STUDYQURAN:35:37/r2"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w4-interpretation", "word": "رَبَّنَآ (word 4)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "رَبَّنَآ (word 4) · interpretation", "words": ["رَبَّنَآ أَخْرِجْنَا"], "view": "Even if returned to the world, they would repeat the forbidden acts; God therefore rejects their request.", "rows": ["IBNKATHIR-FULL:v6p552#3/r1", "STUDYQURAN:35:37/r3"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w4-interpretation", "word": "رَبَّنَآ (word 4)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "رَبَّنَآ (word 4) · interpretation", "words": ["رَبَّنَآ أَخْرِجْنَا نَعْمَلْ صَٰلِحًا"], "view": "Unlike believers who credit divine grace and see their works as small beside God's blessings, the condemned ask to return and work while failing to recognize the majesty that makes their proposed deeds inadequate.", "rows": ["RAZI-FULL:v26p26#3/r10", "RAZI-FULL:v26p26#3/r11", "RAZI-FULL:v26p26#3/r8", "RAZI-FULL:v26p26#3/r9"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w4-links", "word": "رَبَّنَآ (word 4)", "type": "links", "topic": "رَبَّنَآ (word 4) · links", "words": ["رَبَّنَآ أَخْرِجْنَا"], "view": "Their plea belongs to the Qurʾānic accounts of the damned asking for another chance and may form part of an extended exchange with God; their speech precedes the command in 23:108 to stop speaking.", "rows": ["YAHYA-SALLAM:v2p793/r14", "RAZI-FULL:v26p26#3/r4", "KURANYOLU-TEFSIR:35:36/r1", "STUDYQURAN:35:37/r1", "STUDYQURAN:35:37/r5"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w4-links", "word": "رَبَّنَآ (word 4)", "type": "links", "topic": "رَبَّنَآ (word 4) · links", "words": ["رَبَّنَآ أَخْرِجْنَا"], "view": "The claim that those blind in worldly life remain blind in the afterlife explains the futility of their request to return.", "rows": ["RAZI-FULL:v26p26#3/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w6-grammar", "word": "نَعْمَلْ (word 6)", "type": "grammar", "topic": "نَعْمَلْ (word 6) · grammar", "words": ["نَعْمَلْ صَٰلِحًا"], "view": "The jussive verb expresses the result of the request: if You release us, we will do righteous work.", "rows": ["IBNASHUR-FULL:v22p318/r8"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w6-interpretation", "word": "نَعْمَلْ (word 6)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "نَعْمَلْ (word 6) · interpretation", "words": ["نَعْمَلْ صَٰلِحًا غَيْرَ ٱلَّذِى كُنَّا نَعْمَلُ"], "view": "They promise faith and obedience in place of their former disbelief, polytheism, and disobedience; this includes obeying the messengers, and faith is prerequisite for accepted deeds.", "rows": ["MUQATIL:35:37-39/r1", "TAB-FULL:v19p384/r2", "MAWARDI-FULL:v4p476/r2", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v18p432/r4", "TABRISI:35:36-37/r6", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v6p494/r1", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#2/r3", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v9p36/r8", "BURSEVI:v7p277#2/r2", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p200#2/r6"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w6-interpretation", "word": "نَعْمَلْ (word 6)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "نَعْمَلْ (word 6) · interpretation", "words": ["نَعْمَلْ صَٰلِحًا"], "view": "Ibn ʿAbbās identifies the promised righteous deed specifically as professing that there is no god but God.", "rows": ["WAHIDI-BASIT:v18p432/r4", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#2/r2", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v9p36/r8", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p200#2/r7"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w6-theology", "word": "نَعْمَلْ (word 6)", "type": "theology", "topic": "نَعْمَلْ (word 6) · theology", "words": ["نَعْمَلْ صَٰلِحًا"], "view": "Their unqualified promise to do good omits dependence on God and betrays reliance on their own power.", "rows": ["RAZI-FULL:v26p26#3/r6"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w7-grammar", "word": "صَٰلِحًا (word 7)", "type": "grammar", "topic": "صَٰلِحًا (word 7) · grammar", "words": ["صَٰلِحًا غَيْرَ ٱلَّذِى كُنَّا نَعْمَلُ"], "view": "Ṣāliḥan and ghayra may both qualify omitted nouns, or ṣāliḥan may qualify an omitted verbal noun while ghayra serves as the object of 'do.'", "rows": ["SAMIN-DURR:35:37/r3", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p200#2/r5"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w8-rhetoric", "word": "غَيْرَ (word 8)", "type": "rhetoric", "topic": "غَيْرَ (word 8) · rhetoric", "words": ["غَيْرَ ٱلَّذِى كُنَّا نَعْمَلُ"], "view": "The added phrase admits former deeds were wrong and heightens regret. It may imply they had wrongly considered their earlier conduct righteous or followed whim and opposition.", "rows": ["RAZI-FULL:v26p26#3/r7", "BAYDAWI-FULL:35:37/r2", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v9p36/r9", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v9p36/r10", "SAMIN-DURR:35:37/r4", "BIQAI-FULL:v6p229/r1", "BURSEVI:v7p277#2/r3", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p200#2/r4", "IBNASHUR-FULL:v22p318/r9"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w12-rhetoric", "word": "أَوَلَمْ (word 12)", "type": "rhetoric", "topic": "أَوَلَمْ (word 12) · rhetoric", "words": ["أَوَلَمْ نُعَمِّرْكُم"], "view": "The question is a censure and affirmative reminder, answering their plea: they were granted sufficient life to repent and heed guidance, so their request is rebuked.", "rows": ["MUQATIL:35:37-39/r2", "TAB-FULL:v19p387#2/r3", "ZAJJAJ:v4p271/r2", "QUSHAYRI:v3p71/r1", "JISHUMI:v8p5857/r2", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v4p440#2/r8", "TABRISI:35:36-37/r6", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v6p494/r2", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#2/r4", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v9p36/r11", "BURSEVI:v7p277#2/r4", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p200#2/r8", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-6-2:p361/r3", "TABATABAI:35:37-38/r2"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w12-interpretation", "word": "أَوَلَمْ (word 12)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "أَوَلَمْ (word 12) · interpretation", "words": ["أَوَلَمْ نُعَمِّرْكُم مَّا يَتَذَكَّرُ فِيهِ مَن تَذَكَّرَ"], "view": "The allotted time sufficed for any willing person to reflect, heed the evidence, amend conduct, and repent; longer life strengthens the rebuke.", "rows": ["TAB-FULL:v19p387#2/r3", "QUSHAYRI:v3p71/r2", "NASAFI-FULL:v3p345#2/r2", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v6p552#3/r2", "BIQAI-FULL:v6p229/r2", "BURSEVI:v7p277#2/r4", "BURSEVI:v7p277#2/r5", "BURSEVI:v7p277#2/r6", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p200#2/r9", "IBNASHUR-FULL:v22p319/r2"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w12-interpretation", "word": "أَوَلَمْ (word 12)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "أَوَلَمْ (word 12) · interpretation", "words": ["أَوَلَمْ نُعَمِّرْكُم"], "view": "The lifespan itself is evidence against the damned and leaves disbelief without excuse; God's postponement allowed reflection, while after resurrection the opportunity has closed.", "rows": ["IBNABIHATIM:v10p3184#2/r5", "JISHUMI:v8p5857/r1", "BIQAI-FULL:v6p229/r2", "DURR-FULL:v7p31/r3", "ELMALILI:35:32-37/r11"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w12-interpretation", "word": "أَوَلَمْ (word 12)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "أَوَلَمْ (word 12) · interpretation", "words": ["أَوَلَمْ نُعَمِّرْكُم"], "view": "God supplied both inward ability to reflect and external guidance; failure arose from neglect of revelation, not absence of recited guidance.", "rows": ["RAZI-FULL:v26p27/r1"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w12-interpretation", "word": "أَوَلَمْ (word 12)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "أَوَلَمْ (word 12) · interpretation", "words": ["أَوَلَمْ نُعَمِّرْكُم"], "view": "The stated sufficient term applies to those who die after puberty; those who die before maturity receive more lenient treatment.", "rows": ["ELMALILI:35:32-37/r9", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-6-2:p361/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w12-interpretation", "word": "أَوَلَمْ (word 12)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "أَوَلَمْ (word 12) · interpretation", "words": ["أَوَلَمْ نُعَمِّرْكُم"], "view": "Masrūq cautions those who reach forty to be mindful of God; reaching sixty nears death and calls for repentance, humility, and preparation to meet God.", "rows": ["TAB-FULL:v19p384#2/r2", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#2/r8"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w12-theology", "word": "أَوَلَمْ (word 12)", "type": "theology", "topic": "أَوَلَمْ (word 12) · theology", "words": ["أَوَلَمْ نُعَمِّرْكُم"], "view": "Questioning people for their conduct and citing their lifetime as evidence imply that they possessed choice and capacity to act.", "rows": ["JISHUMI:v8p5857/r3"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w13-meaning", "word": "نُعَمِّرْكُم (word 13)", "type": "meaning", "topic": "نُعَمِّرْكُم (word 13) · meaning", "words": ["نُعَمِّرْكُم"], "view": "Taʿmīr means extending a person's life.", "rows": ["IBNASHUR-FULL:v22p319/r1"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-grammar", "word": "مَّا (word 14)", "type": "grammar", "topic": "مَّا (word 14) · grammar", "words": ["مَّا يَتَذَكَّرُ فِيهِ مَن تَذَكَّرَ"], "view": "Mā denotes a period or indefinite span of time in which a person can remember; Ibn ʿAṭiyya and Ibn ʿĀshūr describe a temporal expression.", "rows": ["IBNATIYYA-FULL:v4p440#2/r8", "BURSEVI:v7p277#2/r4", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p200#2/r9", "IBNASHUR-FULL:v22p319/r1", "IBNASHUR-FULL:v22p319/r2", "SAMIN-DURR:35:37/r7"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-grammar", "word": "مَّا (word 14)", "type": "grammar", "topic": "مَّا (word 14) · grammar", "words": ["مَّا يَتَذَكَّرُ فِيهِ مَن تَذَكَّرَ"], "view": "One parse treats mā as a temporal verbal noun meaning the duration of remembering; al-Samīn rejects it because fīhi refers back to mā unless such a verbal noun functions as a noun. Al-Ālūsī records the same objection and a possible implied referent.", "rows": ["SAMIN-DURR:35:37/r5", "SAMIN-DURR:35:37/r6", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p200#2/r10"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-grammar", "word": "مَّا (word 14)", "type": "grammar", "topic": "مَّا (word 14) · grammar", "words": ["مَّا يَتَذَكَّرُ فِيهِ مَن تَذَكَّرَ"], "view": "Treating mā as a negative particle is rejected as untenable in wording and meaning.", "rows": ["ALUSI-FULL:v22p201/r1"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-readings", "word": "مَّا (word 14)", "type": "readings", "topic": "مَّا (word 14) · readings", "words": ["مَّا يَتَذَكَّرُ فِيهِ مَن تَذَكَّرَ"], "view": "The common reading has mā yatadhakkaru fīhi man tadhakkar; al-Aʿmash reads an assimilated form from idhkar, with a linking hamza reportedly pronounced in connected recitation.", "rows": ["IBNATIYYA-FULL:v4p441/r6", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v9p36/r12", "SAMIN-DURR:35:37/r8", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p201/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-referent", "word": "مَّا (word 14)", "type": "referent", "topic": "مَّا (word 14) · referent", "words": ["مَّا يَتَذَكَّرُ فِيهِ مَن تَذَكَّرَ"], "view": "The sufficient span starts at puberty or maturity, the first stage of discernment and responsible reflection.", "rows": ["MAWARDI-FULL:v4p476/r3", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v6p425/r1", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v4p440#2/r9", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v9p36#2/r1", "BURSEVI:v7p277#2/r6", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p201/r3", "ELMALILI:35:32-37/r8"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-referent", "word": "مَّا (word 14)", "type": "referent", "topic": "مَّا (word 14) · referent", "words": ["مَّا يَتَذَكَّرُ فِيهِ مَن تَذَكَّرَ"], "view": "One reported threshold is seventeen years.", "rows": ["ZAJJAJ:v4p271/r3", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v4p440#2/r12", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v9p36#2/r4", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p201/r3"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-referent", "word": "مَّا (word 14)", "type": "referent", "topic": "مَّا (word 14) · referent", "words": ["مَّا يَتَذَكَّرُ فِيهِ مَن تَذَكَّرَ"], "view": "One reported threshold is eighteen years; some reports describe an eighteen-year-old present or the person to whom the rebuke applied when the verse was revealed.", "rows": ["YAHYA-SALLAM:v2p793/r13", "IBNABIHATIM:v10p3184#2/r6", "THALABI:v8p114/r3", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v18p432/r5", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v6p425/r1", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v4p440#2/r10", "TABRISI:35:37-40/r2", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v6p494/r6", "NASAFI-FULL:v3p345#2/r3", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v9p36#2/r2", "DURR-FULL:v7p31/r3", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p201/r3", "TABATABAI:35:37/r5", "ZAJJAJ:v4p271/r3"], "note": ""}
