{"cell": "w14-referent", "word": "مَّا (word 14)", "type": "referent", "topic": "مَّا (word 14) · referent", "words": ["مَّا يَتَذَكَّرُ فِيهِ مَن تَذَكَّرَ"], "view": "One report treats any age from twenty through sixty as a sufficient period.", "rows": ["ALUSI-FULL:v22p201/r3", "ELMALILI:35:32-37/r8"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-referent", "word": "مَّا (word 14)", "type": "referent", "topic": "مَّا (word 14) · referent", "words": ["مَّا يَتَذَكَّرُ فِيهِ مَن تَذَكَّرَ"], "view": "Another view sets the period at seventy, the last time for reflection before senility.", "rows": ["MAWARDI-FULL:v4p476/r6", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v6p494/r3", "BURSEVI:v7p277#2/r8"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-reports", "word": "مَّا (word 14)", "type": "reports", "topic": "مَّا (word 14) · reports", "words": ["مَّا يَتَذَكَّرُ فِيهِ مَن تَذَكَّرَ"], "view": "Prophetic reports say that reaching sixty, or in some transmissions sixty or seventy, removes a person's excuse because God has granted ample life and warning; al-Bukhārī titled a chapter accordingly, and Ibn Kathīr accepts the hadith through several routes.", "rows": ["ABDURRAZZAQ:v3p138/r2", "TAB-FULL:v19p384#2/r6", "TAB-FULL:v19p384#2/r7", "IBNABIHATIM:v10p3184#2/r3", "IBNABIHATIM:v10p3184#2/r8", "THALABI:v8p114/r7", "MAWARDI-FULL:v4p476/r7", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v18p433/r3", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v6p425/r2", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v4p441/r5", "TABRISI:35:37-40/r1", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#2/r5", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#2/r6", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#2/r7", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#2/r8", "BAYDAWI-FULL:35:37/r4", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v6p553/r6", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v6p554/r1", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v6p554/r2", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v6p554/r3", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v6p554/r4", "BIQAI-FULL:v6p229/r4", "DURR-FULL:v7p30/r5", "DURR-FULL:v7p31/r1", "BURSEVI:v7p277#2/r7", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p201/r2", "TABATABAI:35:37/r3"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-reports", "word": "مَّا (word 14)", "type": "reports", "topic": "مَّا (word 14) · reports", "words": ["مَّا يَتَذَكَّرُ فِيهِ مَن تَذَكَّرَ"], "view": "Reports say a caller on Judgment Day summons those who reached sixty and cites this verse; Ibn Kathīr questions one route because of Ibrāhīm ibn al-Faḍl.", "rows": ["MUJAHID:v2p532#2/r1", "TAB-FULL:v19p384#2/r5", "IBNABIHATIM:v10p3184#2/r2", "THALABI:v8p114/r6", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v4p441/r4", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#2/r10", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#2/r11", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v6p553/r4", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v6p553/r5", "DURR-FULL:v7p30/r4", "TABATABAI:35:37/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-reports", "word": "مَّا (word 14)", "type": "reports", "topic": "مَّا (word 14) · reports", "words": ["مَّا يَتَذَكَّرُ فِيهِ مَن تَذَكَّرَ"], "view": "Reports place most of the Prophet's community's lifespans and deaths between sixty and seventy, with few exceeding that; Ibn Kathīr calls one chain weak, while al-Tirmidhī calls another ḥasan gharīb and al-Bazzār flags a weak transmitter.", "rows": ["THALABI:v8p114/r8", "JISHUMI:v8p5855/r6", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v6p425/r3", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#3/r2", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v6p555/r1", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v6p555/r3", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v6p556/r1", "BIQAI-FULL:v6p229/r5", "DURR-FULL:v7p31/r1", "BURSEVI:v7p277#2/r8"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-reports", "word": "مَّا (word 14)", "type": "reports", "topic": "مَّا (word 14) · reports", "words": ["مَّا يَتَذَكَّرُ فِيهِ مَن تَذَكَّرَ"], "view": "A report gives the community's lifespan as fifty to sixty years and invokes mercy on those reaching seventy or eighty.", "rows": ["IBNKATHIR-FULL:v6p556/r2"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-reports", "word": "مَّا (word 14)", "type": "reports", "topic": "مَّا (word 14) · reports", "words": ["مَّا يَتَذَكَّرُ فِيهِ مَن تَذَكَّرَ"], "view": "Physicians cited by Ibn Kathīr propose a natural lifespan of 120 years, with growth until sixty and decline afterward; a poem depicts the loss of youthful pleasure at sixty.", "rows": ["IBNKATHIR-FULL:v6p555/r2"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-reports", "word": "مَّا (word 14)", "type": "reports", "topic": "مَّا (word 14) · reports", "words": ["مَّا يَتَذَكَّرُ فِيهِ مَن تَذَكَّرَ"], "view": "The Prophet's lifespan is most often given as sixty-three years, though reports also say sixty and sixty-five.", "rows": ["IBNKATHIR-FULL:v6p556/r3"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-reports", "word": "مَّا (word 14)", "type": "reports", "topic": "مَّا (word 14) · reports", "words": ["مَّا يَتَذَكَّرُ فِيهِ مَن تَذَكَّرَ"], "view": "Reports describe people turning more wholly toward worship and the hereafter at forty; a poem warns that one still without restraint at forty has chosen his path.", "rows": ["WAHIDI-BASIT:v18p433/r1", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v4p441/r1", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#3/r1", "BURSEVI:v7p278/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-reports", "word": "مَّا (word 14)", "type": "reports", "topic": "مَّا (word 14) · reports", "words": ["مَّا يَتَذَكَّرُ فِيهِ مَن تَذَكَّرَ"], "view": "A daily and nightly caller reportedly warns at forty that harvest nears, at sixty to account for deeds, and at seventy to face reckoning.", "rows": ["BURSEVI:v7p277#2/r9"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-inward", "word": "مَّا (word 14)", "type": "inward", "topic": "مَّا (word 14) · inward", "words": ["مَّا يَتَذَكَّرُ فِيهِ مَن تَذَكَّرَ"], "view": "ʿAbd al-Qādir tells a young penitent that God preserved and drew him near despite earlier estrangement, and an old penitent that pardon and delay remain open to return despite displeasure in old age.", "rows": ["BURSEVI:v7p278/r1", "BURSEVI:v7p278/r2"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w14-inward", "word": "مَّا (word 14)", "type": "inward", "topic": "مَّا (word 14) · inward", "words": ["مَّا يَتَذَكَّرُ فِيهِ مَن تَذَكَّرَ"], "view": "A Persian couplet contrasts young people hastening toward spiritual gain with the hindrance of old age; death's hidden time means no age is safe.", "rows": ["BURSEVI:v7p278/r3", "BURSEVI:v7p278/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-meaning", "word": "مَن (word 17)", "type": "meaning", "topic": "مَن (word 17) · meaning", "words": ["مِن نَّصِيرٍ"], "view": "Proof may be called sulṭān because authority or power provides aid.", "rows": ["RAZI-FULL:v26p27/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w17-rhetoric", "word": "مَن (word 17)", "type": "rhetoric", "topic": "مَن (word 17) · rhetoric", "words": ["مِن نَّصِيرٍ"], "view": "The singular helper fits their situation after despair of human allies and idols, when they hope only for God; other passages depict earlier expectations of idol-help.", "rows": ["RAZI-FULL:v26p27/r5"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w19-grammar", "word": "وَجَآءَكُمُ (word 19)", "type": "grammar", "topic": "وَجَآءَكُمُ (word 19) · grammar", "words": ["وَجَآءَكُمُ ٱلنَّذِيرُ"], "view": "'The warner came to you' coordinates with the affirmative sense of 'Did We not give you life?' as 'We gave you life, and the warner came'; another parse coordinates with its form.", "rows": ["NASAFI-FULL:v3p345#2/r4", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v9p36#2/r5", "SAMIN-DURR:35:37#2/r1", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p201/r5", "IBNASHUR-FULL:v22p319/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w19-readings", "word": "وَجَآءَكُمُ (word 19)", "type": "readings", "topic": "وَجَآءَكُمُ (word 19) · readings", "words": ["وَجَآءَكُمُ ٱلنَّذِيرُ"], "view": "An alternate recitation reads the warning term in the plural, al-nudhur, instead of the singular nadhīr.", "rows": ["QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#3/r3", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v9p36#2/r6", "SAMIN-DURR:35:37#2/r3"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w19-interpretation", "word": "وَجَآءَكُمُ (word 19)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "وَجَآءَكُمُ (word 19) · interpretation", "words": ["وَجَآءَكُمُ ٱلنَّذِيرُ"], "view": "Long life and the messengers together were evidence against them; messengers and books supplied warning beyond what reason alone established.", "rows": ["IBNABIHATIM:v10p3184#2/r7", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v6p556/r6", "BIQAI-FULL:v6p229/r6", "DURR-FULL:v7p31/r3", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-6-2:p361/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w19-law", "word": "وَجَآءَكُمُ (word 19)", "type": "law", "topic": "وَجَآءَكُمُ (word 19) · law", "words": ["وَجَآءَكُمُ ٱلنَّذِيرُ"], "view": "One legal application says Hajj may be delayed while completion remains likely; sudden death incurs no sin, whereas a clear warning that delay risks missing it makes postponement impermissible.", "rows": ["BURSEVI:v7p279/r2"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w20-meaning", "word": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20)", "type": "meaning", "topic": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20) · meaning", "words": ["ٱلنَّذِيرُ"], "view": "Nadhīr can mean a warning rather than a particular warning-bearer.", "rows": ["QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#3/r7"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w20-grammar", "word": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20)", "type": "grammar", "topic": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20) · grammar", "words": ["ٱلنَّذِيرُ"], "view": "If nadhīr denotes Muhammad it is an active participle; if it denotes gray hair it is better read as a verbal noun. Its singular form suits the immediate context.", "rows": ["WAHIDI-BASIT:v18p433/r6", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p201/r8"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w20-referent", "word": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20)", "type": "referent", "topic": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20) · referent", "words": ["ٱلنَّذِيرُ"], "view": "The warner is Muhammad, the messenger whose warning makes people responsible; identifying him stresses the warning aspect of his mission, and some cite other verses calling him a warner.", "rows": ["MUQATIL:35:37-39/r2", "YAHYA-SALLAM:v2p793/r12", "IBNQUTAYBA-GHARIB:v1p361#9/r1", "TAB-FULL:v19p387#2/r1", "ZAJJAJ:v4p271/r4", "IBNABIHATIM:v10p3184#2/r9", "IBNABIHATIM:v10p3184#2/r10", "THALABI:v8p114/r9", "MAWARDI-FULL:v4p476/r8", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v18p433/r4", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v18p433/r7", "WAHIDI-WAJIZ:35:34-37/r5", "JISHUMI:v8p5855/r7", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v6p425#2/r1", "TABRISI:35:37-40/r3", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v6p494/r8", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#3/r5", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#3/r13", "NASAFI-FULL:v3p345#2/r4", "BAYDAWI-FULL:35:37/r3", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v6p556/r5", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v6p556/r6", "DURR-FULL:v7p31/r4", "BURSEVI:v7p278/r5", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p201/r6", "IBNASHUR-FULL:v22p319/r3"], "note": "The competing identifications are the Qur'an, all prophets, gray hair, reason and signs of mortality."}
{"cell": "w20-referent", "word": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20)", "type": "referent", "topic": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20) · referent", "words": ["ٱلنَّذِيرُ"], "view": "The singular warner is generic for prophets: each prophet warned his contemporaries, with Muhammad warning later people.", "rows": ["IBNATIYYA-FULL:v4p441/r7", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v9p36#2/r6", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p201/r6"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w20-referent", "word": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20)", "type": "referent", "topic": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20) · referent", "words": ["ٱلنَّذِيرُ"], "view": "The warner is the Qurʾān or revealed scripture.", "rows": ["THALABI:v8p114/r9", "JISHUMI:v8p5855/r8", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v6p425#2/r1", "TABRISI:35:37-40/r3", "TABRISI:35:37-40/r4", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#3/r4", "BAYDAWI-FULL:35:37/r3", "BURSEVI:v7p278/r5", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p201/r6"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w20-referent", "word": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20)", "type": "referent", "topic": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20) · referent", "words": ["ٱلنَّذِيرُ"], "view": "The warner is gray hair, a visible sign of advancing age and approaching death; poetry and a saying about each white hair reinforce this usage.", "rows": ["MUJAHID:v2p532#2/r2", "IBNQUTAYBA-GHARIB:v1p361#9/r2", "TAB-FULL:v19p387#2/r2", "ZAJJAJ:v4p271/r4", "IBNABIHATIM:v10p3185/r1", "THALABI:v8p114/r10", "THALABI:v8p114/r11", "MAWARDI-FULL:v4p476/r9", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v18p433/r5", "WAHIDI-WAJIZ:35:34-37/r6", "JISHUMI:v8p5855/r9", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v6p425#2/r2", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v6p425#2/r3", "IBNATIYYA-FULL:v4p441/r8", "TABRISI:35:37-40/r3", "TABRISI:35:37-40/r4", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v6p494/r7", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#3/r6", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#3/r9", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#3/r10", "BAYDAWI-FULL:35:37/r3", "NASAFI-FULL:v3p345#2/r4", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v9p36#2/r7", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v6p556/r4", "DURR-FULL:v7p31/r5", "BURSEVI:v7p278/r5", "BURSEVI:v7p278/r6", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p201/r7"], "note": "Ibn ʿAṭiyya calls this apt but says binding proof comes through scriptural warning."}
{"cell": "w20-referent", "word": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20)", "type": "referent", "topic": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20) · referent", "words": ["ٱلنَّذِيرُ"], "view": "The warner may be fever, which heralds death.", "rows": ["MAWARDI-FULL:v4p476/r10", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v6p494/r9", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#3/r7", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#3/r8", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p201/r8"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w20-referent", "word": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20)", "type": "referent", "topic": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20) · referent", "words": ["ٱلنَّذِيرُ"], "view": "The warner may be the deaths of relatives, friends, or neighbors, repeatedly reminding survivors of their own departure; poetry illustrates the point.", "rows": ["MAWARDI-FULL:v4p476/r10", "TABRISI:35:37-40/r3", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v6p494/r9", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#3/r7", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#3/r8", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#3/r11", "BAYDAWI-FULL:35:37/r3", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v9p36#2/r7", "BURSEVI:v7p278/r5", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p201/r8"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w20-referent", "word": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20)", "type": "referent", "topic": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20) · referent", "words": ["ٱلنَّذِيرُ"], "view": "The warner may be mature reason, by which one discerns reality and moral difference and prepares for the hereafter.", "rows": ["MAWARDI-FULL:v4p476/r10", "TABRISI:35:37-40/r3", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#3/r7", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#3/r12", "BAYDAWI-FULL:35:37/r3", "BURSEVI:v7p278/r5", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p201/r8"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w20-referent", "word": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20)", "type": "referent", "topic": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20) · referent", "words": ["ٱلنَّذِيرُ"], "view": "Extreme old age itself may be the warning.", "rows": ["ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v9p36#2/r7"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w20-referent", "word": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20)", "type": "referent", "topic": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20) · referent", "words": ["ٱلنَّذِيرُ"], "view": "One explanation takes the warning as the subsidiary branches of religious rulings.", "rows": ["ELMALILI:35:32-37/r12"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w20-reports", "word": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20)", "type": "reports", "topic": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20) · reports", "words": ["ٱلنَّذِيرُ"], "view": "A report says Abraham was the first descendant of Adam to gray; God called gray hair dignity in this world and light in the next, and Abraham asked for more.", "rows": ["BURSEVI:v7p278/r7"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w20-reports", "word": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20)", "type": "reports", "topic": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20) · reports", "words": ["ٱلنَّذِيرُ"], "view": "A reported hadith says God dislikes an elderly man whose hair has not turned gray.", "rows": ["BURSEVI:v7p278/r8"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w20-interpretation", "word": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20) · interpretation", "words": ["ٱلنَّذِيرُ"], "view": "Gray hair warns that youth and its play have passed, prompting preparation for death.", "rows": ["THALABI:v8p114/r10", "THALABI:v8p114/r11", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#3/r9", "BURSEVI:v7p278/r6"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w20-interpretation", "word": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "ٱلنَّذِيرُ (word 20) · interpretation", "words": ["ٱلنَّذِيرُ"], "view": "Every sign of impending departure from life can count as a warner calling for heedfulness.", "rows": ["QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#3/r8", "BURSEVI:v7p279/r1"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w21-rhetoric", "word": "فَذُوقُوا۟ (word 21)", "type": "rhetoric", "topic": "فَذُوقُوا۟ (word 21) · rhetoric", "words": ["فَذُوقُوا۟"], "view": "The imperative 'taste' humiliates the damned and signals enduring punishment; its object, punishment, is omitted.", "rows": ["RAZI-FULL:v26p27/r2", "IBNASHUR-FULL:v22p319/r5"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w21-interpretation", "word": "فَذُوقُوا۟ (word 21)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "فَذُوقُوا۟ (word 21) · interpretation", "words": ["فَذُوقُوا۟"], "view": "The command orders them to taste Hell's punishment, with remorse and continuing torment; its fāʾ makes that punishment the consequence of their failure to heed their lifetime and the warning.", "rows": ["YAHYA-SALLAM:v2p794/r1", "TAB-FULL:v19p388/r1", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v18p433/r8", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v6p425#2/r4", "TABRISI:35:37-40/r5", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v6p495/r1", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#4/r1", "ABUHAYYAN-FULL:v9p36#2/r8", "RAZI-FULL:v26p27/r2", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v6p556#2/r1", "BIQAI-FULL:v6p229/r6", "BURSEVI:v7p279/r4", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p201/r9", "IBNASHUR-FULL:v22p319/r5", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-6-2:p361/r3", "TABATABAI:35:37-38/r2"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w21-inward", "word": "فَذُوقُوا۟ (word 21)", "type": "inward", "topic": "فَذُوقُوا۟ (word 21) · inward", "words": ["فَذُوقُوا۟"], "view": "In an ishārī reading, people sleep in worldly heedlessness and wake fully after death and resurrection, when they perceive the punishment they taste.", "rows": ["BURSEVI:v7p279/r5"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w22-grammar", "word": "فَمَا (word 22)", "type": "grammar", "topic": "فَمَا (word 22) · grammar", "words": ["فَمَا لِلظَّٰلِمِينَ مِن نَّصِيرٍ"], "view": "Min naṣīr may be a subject governed by the preposition or a topic whose predicate is the preceding prepositional phrase.", "rows": ["SAMIN-DURR:35:37#2/r2"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w22-rhetoric", "word": "فَمَا (word 22)", "type": "rhetoric", "topic": "فَمَا (word 22) · rhetoric", "words": ["فَمَا لِلظَّٰلِمِينَ مِن نَّصِيرٍ"], "view": "The denial of help may continue the rebuke to the damned and end hope of rescue, or it may be an independent conclusion for listeners applying to every wrongdoer.", "rows": ["IBNASHUR-FULL:v22p320/r1", "IBNASHUR-FULL:v22p320/r2", "BIQAI-FULL:v6p229/r7"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w22-interpretation", "word": "فَمَا (word 22)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "فَمَا (word 22) · interpretation", "words": ["فَمَا لِلظَّٰلِمِينَ مِن نَّصِيرٍ"], "view": "No one can defend or rescue the wrongdoers from God's punishment, restraints, and chains; their former allies and idols cannot help.", "rows": ["MUQATIL:35:37-39/r2", "YAHYA-SALLAM:v2p794/r2", "TAB-FULL:v19p388/r1", "WAHIDI-BASIT:v18p433/r8", "BAGHAWI-FULL:v6p425#2/r4", "TABRISI:35:37-40/r5", "IBNJAWZI-ZAD:v6p495/r1", "QURTUBI-FULL:35:36-37#4/r2", "BAYDAWI-FULL:35:37/r5", "NASAFI-FULL:v3p345#2/r5", "RAZI-FULL:v26p27/r4", "IBNKATHIR-FULL:v6p556#2/r1", "BIQAI-FULL:v6p229/r6", "BURSEVI:v7p279/r4", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p201/r9", "ISLAHI-TADABBUR:vol-6-2:p361/r3", "TABATABAI:35:37-38/r2", "TABATABAI:35:37-38/r3"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w22-interpretation", "word": "فَمَا (word 22)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "فَمَا (word 22) · interpretation", "words": ["فَمَا لِلظَّٰلِمِينَ مِن نَّصِيرٍ"], "view": "Al-Rāzī's preferred broad reading excludes all help, from God or anyone else.", "rows": ["RAZI-FULL:v26p27/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w22-interpretation", "word": "فَمَا (word 22)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "فَمَا (word 22) · interpretation", "words": ["فَمَا لِلظَّٰلِمِينَ مِن نَّصِيرٍ"], "view": "An alternative says the wrongdoer's compounded ignorance, mistaking falsehood for truth, leaves him without beneficial knowledge in the afterlife.", "rows": ["RAZI-FULL:v26p27/r3"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w22-interpretation", "word": "فَمَا (word 22)", "type": "interpretation", "topic": "فَمَا (word 22) · interpretation", "words": ["فَمَا لِلظَّٰلِمِينَ مِن نَّصِيرٍ"], "view": "Their lack of helpers follows from turning away from God and the help He sent during worldly life.", "rows": ["STUDYQURAN:35:37/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w22-theology", "word": "فَمَا (word 22)", "type": "theology", "topic": "فَمَا (word 22) · theology", "words": ["فَمَا لِلظَّٰلِمِينَ مِن نَّصِيرٍ"], "view": "One theological reading concludes that major sinners receive no intercession.", "rows": ["JISHUMI:v8p5857/r4"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w22-law", "word": "فَمَا (word 22)", "type": "law", "topic": "فَمَا (word 22) · law", "words": ["فَمَا لِلظَّٰلِمِينَ مِن نَّصِيرٍ"], "view": "Because aiding oppression violates justice, the community should restrain wrongdoing; a Prophetic report explains that helping an unjust person means stopping his injustice.", "rows": ["IBNASHUR-FULL:v22p320/r4", "IBNASHUR-FULL:v22p320/r5"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w23-meaning", "word": "لِلظَّٰلِمِينَ (word 23)", "type": "meaning", "topic": "لِلظَّٰلِمِينَ (word 23) · meaning", "words": ["ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ"], "view": "Wrongdoing violates another's due; its gravest form is shirk, which affronts God's oneness and harms the self by bringing punishment.", "rows": ["IBNASHUR-FULL:v22p320/r3"], "note": ""}
{"cell": "w23-referent", "word": "لِلظَّٰلِمِينَ (word 23)", "type": "referent", "topic": "لِلظَّٰلِمِينَ (word 23) · referent", "words": ["ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ"], "view": "The wrongdoers here are unbelievers and polytheists who wronged themselves through disbelief and idolatry.", "rows": ["YAHYA-SALLAM:v2p794/r2", "TAB-FULL:v19p388/r1", "BURSEVI:v7p279/r4", "ALUSI-FULL:v22p201/r9", "IBNASHUR-FULL:v22p320/r3"], "note": ""}
